{"artifact_digest":"sha256:a57b131ccb7f86debdc0c9634b5a1106be4417237ee73e1d811322c6cb6a4990","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/a5/a57b131ccb7f86debdc0c9634b5a1106be4417237ee73e1d811322c6cb6a4990.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:909fab6f86fab97e93cf4400f54a2def74dd5cb791f32f2557a839c5726a1995","bundle_entry_key":"2609-03869-lemma-10-lem-analysis-of-lambda","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_165","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_165.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-03869-lem-10-lem-analysis-of-lambda","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: \textit{Proof of (i)}.	Let us first claim that $\Re\lambda(\xi)\le 0$ for all $\xi\in\R$.
	Assume by contradiction that the solution $\lambda_0:=\lambda(\xi_0)\in\mathbb{C}$ to \eqref{A4} associated with some $\xi_0\in\R$ satisfies $\Re\lambda_0>0$. It is easily seen that $|\widehat{\K_*}(\xi_0)|=\Big|\int_\R e^{-\mathbf{i}x\xi_0}\K_*(x)\md x\Big|\le\widehat{\K_*}(0)$, and
	\begin{equation*}
