[Lemma lem-u-bar is a semimartingale of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] The process $\duality{\overline{u}}{\phi}\coloneqq \bigl\{\duality{\overline{u}(t)}{\phi}:\, t\in [0,T]\bigr\}$
is a $\mathbb{R}$-valued semimartingale.
Moreover, its quadratic variation process is equal to the quadratic variation process of the process $\fourIdx{}{}{}{\phi}{\overline{M}}$, i.e.\ $\overline{\mathbb{P}}$-a.s.
\begin{equation}
[\duality{\overline{u}}{\phi},\duality{\overline{u}}{\phi}](t) =[\fourIdx{}{}{}{\phi}{\overline{M}},\fourIdx{}{}{}{\phi}{\overline{M}}](t), \;\; t\in [0,T].
\end{equation}

[Prop cmj-package of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Fix $\varepsilon\in(0,1/2)$ and $y\in\mathds{R}$.
There exist non-negative random variables $W_{1,n},W_{2,n}$, defined on the probability space carrying the coupling above, such that
\begin{align}
 (W_{1,n},W_{2,n})\Rightarrow(W_1,W_2),
\end{align}
and, for $i=1,2$,
\begin{align}
 \sup_{\mathfrak{s}_0\leqslant s\leqslant \mathfrak{s}_1}
 \abs{e^{-s}N_i(s)-W_{i,n}}
 \stackrel{\pr}{\to}0.
\end{align}
Moreover, if
\begin{align*}
 A_v^{(i)}(s)
 :=s-\mathfrak{a}_\ell\widehat\mathsf{T}_i(v),
 \qquad
 v\in\mathcal{C}_i(s),
\end{align*}
then, for every continuous $g$ satisfying $|g(a)|\leqslant Ce^{\eta a}$ for some $\eta<1$, and also for every bounded Riemann-integrable $g$,
\begin{align}
 \sup_{\mathfrak{s}_0\leqslant s\leqslant \mathfrak{s}_1}
 \abs{
 \frac1{N_i(s)}
 \sum_{v\in\mathcal{C}_i(s)}g\bigl(A_v^{(i)}(s)\bigr)
 -\int_0^\infty g(a)e^{-a}\,\mathrm d a
 }
 \stackrel{\pr}{\to}0.
\end{align}
For every fixed $k\in\mathds{Z}\setminus\{0\}$ and every bounded Riemann-integrable $g$,
\begin{align}
 \sup_{\mathfrak{s}_0\leqslant s\leqslant \mathfrak{s}_1}
 \abs{
 \frac1{N_i(s)}
 \sum_{v\in\mathcal{C}_i(s)}
 g\bigl(A_v^{(i)}(s)\bigr)e^{2\pi \mathrm{i}kv/n}
 }
 \stackrel{\pr}{\to}0.
\end{align}

