[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2608.21701, 'Superdiffusivity of random walks on the three-dimensional randomly oriented Manhattan latt'] Assume that $R$ is a positive diagonal operator whose multipliers $(\mathfrak r^{(n)})_{n\ge 1}$ satisfy \eqref{eq:R.momentum} and \eqref{eq:R.res}. Then there exists $C<\infty$, depending only on $C_R$, such that, for every $n\ge 1$ and $f\in\ell^2_0(U,3,n)$,
\begin{equation}
\left|\left\langle f, A_-R A_+f\right\rangle_{\ell^2(U,3,n)}-\left(V_{\rm Diag}(R,f)+V_{\rm Off}(R,f)\right)\right|\le\frac{Cn}{\kappa}\langle f,(-S)f\rangle_{\ell^2(U,3,n)} .
\end{equation}

