[Proposition prop:Ylim of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Consider the same notation and conditions as in Proposition~(prop:depthlabelsinglevertex of the paper). Additionally, recall $\mathcal{S}_n^+(a_1)$ from~(equation eq:definition_selection_sets_ungreedy_depth_single_vertex of the paper), fix $y\in \mathbb{R}$ and, conditionally on $\mathcal{S}_n^+(a_1)$, define the random variable
\begin{equation} 
Y_n(y)\sim \mathrm{Bin}\Big(|[L_n(d,y)-1]\cap \mathcal{S}_n^+(a_1)|,\frac{1}{m+1}\Big). 
\end{equation} 
Then, with $N$ a standard normal random variable, 
\begin{equation} 
\frac{Y_n(y)-(mh_n^+-\frac{m}{m+1}d)}{\sqrt{mh_n^+-\frac{m}{(m+1)^2}d}}\buildrel {\mathrm{d}}\over{\longrightarrow}  N\sqrt{1-\frac{mb}{(m+1)^2-b}}+y\sqrt{\frac{mb}{(m+1)^2-b}}.
\end{equation}

