[Proposition prop:invariance of arXiv:2608.17022, 'Sharp hypocoercive convergence estimates for underdamped Langevin dynamics with specular r'] Let $f,g\in\mathscr C$. Then
\begin{equation}
\int_{\Omega\times\mathbb{R}^d}\mathscr{L} f\,\mathrm{d}\mu=0,
\end{equation}
so that $\mu$ is invariant for (equation eq:sde of the paper) and $\Lmuz$ is preserved by the flow; and along any solution of (equation eq:bke of the paper) in $\mathscr C$,
\begin{equation}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} t}\,\frac12\nrm{f(t)}^2=-\gamma\nrm{\nabla_vf(t)}^2\le0 ,
\end{equation}
so the flow is an $\Lmu$-contraction. Moreover $\mathscr{L}$ is reversible up to velocity reversal: writing $(\mathcal Sf)(x,v):=f(x,-v)$, one has $\mathcal S^2=\mathrm{Id}$, $\mathcal S\mathscr C=\mathscr C$, and
\begin{equation}
\mathscr{L}^*=\mathcal S\,\mathscr{L}\,\mathcal S\qquad\text{on }\mathscr C,
\end{equation}
where $\mathscr{L}^*$ is the $\Lmu$-adjoint.

