[Prop 51 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Suppose that $(Z_m)_m$ is locally bounded in $\cM_{\mathrm{adm}}(\cV^{\bar{\zeta}})$ and $f_m\in\cD^{\gamma,\delta}_{T}(Z_m)$ is locally bounded uniformly in $m$.
Then, after passing to a subsequence, there exist $Z\in\cM_{\mathrm{adm}}(\cV^{\bar{\zeta}})$ and $f\in\cD^{\gamma,\delta}_{T}(Z)$ such that
\begin{align*}
    \iota^{\cM}_{\zeta,\bar\zeta}Z_m
    &\longrightarrow
    \iota^{\cM}_{\zeta,\bar\zeta}Z,\qquad
    Q^\zeta_{<\gamma'}
    \iota_{\zeta,\bar\zeta}f_m
    \longrightarrow
    Q^\zeta_{<\gamma'}
    \iota_{\zeta,\bar\zeta}f
\end{align*}
locally in the corresponding model and singular modelled-distribution topologies corresponding to the shift $\zeta$.

