body:
[Lemma CP_lemma of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] There exists a finite constant $C_0$ such that
\begin{align*}
\sup_{\theta\in {\mathbb{T}}}|\,u^{(\epsilon)}(\theta) - \bar{u}_K(\theta)\,|
\, \leq\, C_0 K^{-1/4}\;, \quad
\sup_{\theta\in {\mathbb{T}}} |\, (\partial_\theta u^{(\epsilon)}) (\theta) -
(\partial_\theta \bar{u}_K) (\theta)\, | \, \leq\,  C_0 K^{1/4} 
\end{align*}
For all $K\ge 1$. In this formula, $\epsilon = K^{-1/2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

