\paragraph{\underline{Step 1: the data decay two orders below the target}} By Lemma~(lem:H-decay of the paper) and the strict hypothesis $s>\beta+2$,
\begin{align}
 \abs{H(Y)}\le C\mathcal A_{s}\left\langleR\right\rangle^{-s}
 \le C\mathcal A_{s}\left\langleR\right\rangle^{-\beta-2},
 \qquad Y\in K_\omega .

\end{align}
This is the weight that the barrier defect in (equation eq:global-barrier of the paper) bounds from below, and it is the only place where $s>\beta+2$ is used. The two orders are the diffusive order of $I-\mathsf T_\omega$.

