[Theorem thm:SRW of arXiv:2601.10624, 'Source localisation in simple random walks'] For any infinite vertex-transitive strongly transient graph $\mathbb{H}$ of finite degree,
    \begin{equation*}
        \liminf_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{P}_v\big(\Psi(G_n^\mathbb{H}) = v\big) > 0.
    \end{equation*}
    In particular, source localisation is possible if $\mathbb{H} = \mathbb{Z}^d$ for $d \geqslant 5$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

