[Lemma hnlb of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:geq1 of the paper) is satisfied and integers $1\leq a<b<\infty$. Then, 
\begin{equation} 
h_b^+(\mathbf x)-h^+_{a-1}(\mathbf x)=\sum_{i=a}^b \mathbbm{1}_{\{x_i=1\}}\frac{1}{A_i(\mathbf x)} \geq \log\Big(\frac{b}{2a}\Big). 
\end{equation} 
In particular, with $a=1$ and $b=n$ we obtain~(equation eq:hn+lb of the paper).

