[Lem bigggg-lemma of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] \textcolor{black}{Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a bounded subset in $R_{+}^{K^2+K}$. Then we have 
\begin{align*}
    \sup_{i=0,1,2} \, \sup_{\boldsymbol{x} \in \mathcal{C}}\left|\mathbf{P}_{i,n}(\boldsymbol{x}) - \mathbf{P}_{i+1,n}(\boldsymbol{x}) \right|\leqslant  \frac{C}{n}
\end{align*}for some constant $C \geqslant 0$ depending of the set $\mathcal{C}$ and $K$.} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

