body:
[Lemma laststep of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Let $f:\Omega\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a local function supported in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0-1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$, and assume that $\psi_f(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0$ and $\nabla\psi_f(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0$ for fixed $\rho\in [0,1]$ and $\mathcal{E}\in [\rho ,\kappa\rho]$. Then, there exists a constant~$C_{16}=C_{16}(\kappa ,\rho ,\mathcal{E} ,f)>0$ such that for any $t\in [0,T]$, any $\ell\ge\ell_0$ and any measurable function $v:[0,T]\longrightarrow\ell^2(\mathbb{Z} )$, we have 
    \begin{multline}
        \mathbb{E}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}\left[\left( \int_0^t \sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}} \tau_x\left\{ \mathbb{E}_\ell [f](s)-\frac12 \overline{\mathbf{u}}^\ell (s)^\top\mathrm{Hess}(\psi_f)(\rho ,\mathcal{E})\overline{\mathbf{u}}^\ell (s)\right.\right.\right. \\
        \left.\left.\left. +\frac{1}{2\ell}\mathrm{Tr}(\chi\mathrm{Hess}(\psi_f))(\rho ,\mathcal{E})\right\} v_s(x)\,\mathrm{d} s\right)^2\right] \le \frac{C_{16}}{N^a}\int_0^t\| v_s\|^2\,\mathrm{d} s.
    \end{multline}

