[Definition def:Irb of arXiv:2608.05262, 'The law of $(1+1)$D SOS with an area tilt in a wedge'] Fix $\varepsilon \in (0,\tfrac{1}{9})$, $\Delta=N^{2/3+\varepsilon}$, $a_0^+=N+\Delta$ 
and set
\begin{align*}

\mathfrak I_{\pm r} &:=\pm [a^+_{r}- \Delta,a^+_{r-1}-\Delta)\qquad(1 \le r \le K)\,,\\

\mathfrak I_{K+1} &:= \;\;\, (a^-_K+\Delta,a^+_K-\Delta) \,.
\end{align*}    
Consider the event 
\begin{equation}
A := \{ \underline{\widetilde \phi} (N)=\underline 0\} \cap A^- \cap A^+ \,,
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

A^\pm := \big\{\widetilde \phi_{r} \ge \cdots \ge \widetilde \phi_{K} \ge 0
\quad \mbox{on} \quad \mathfrak I_{\pm r}, \quad \mbox{for} \quad 1 \le r \le K\big\} \,.
\end{equation}
Note that 
$\{\mathfrak I_r\}$ 
partitions $(-N,N)$ into $2K+1$ sub-intervals,
as depicted in (fig:tilde-phi-events-A-B of the paper).

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Suppose that \eqref{t1-1-1} holds for some $\beta>0$. Let $\Upsilon_\e^1 f(x,y)$ be defined by \eqref{l2-1-3a}. Then there exists a positive constant $C_7:=C_7(\beta)$ such that for every $f\in \M_\beta$, $x\in \R^d$ and $y\in \T^d$,
\begin{equation}
|\Upsilon_\e^1 f(x,y)|\le C_7\left(\sum_{i=0}^2\|f\|_{\M_{\beta},i}\right)(1+|x|)^{-d-\beta_0}.
\end{equation}

