[Definition eq:maindeifnition of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be an UPPS. The upper probability $V$ is said to be of finite ergodic components if there exists a partition $\alpha=\{A_1,\ldots,A_n\}\subset \mathcal{I}$, such that for each $i\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}$, $V_i$  is an ergodic upper probability with respect to $T$ on $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$, where 
	\begin{equation}
		V_i(A):=\sup\{P(A):P\in\operatorname{core}(V)\text{ and } P(A_i)=1\}\text{ for any }A\in\mathcal{F}.
	\end{equation}

