[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2608.26628 (problem environment).] Are the following true?
 \begin{enumerate}
 \item[(1)] For any c.e. set $A$, there exists a c.e. set $D\subseteq 2\mathbb{N}$, such that $A\equiv_{rK}D$ and $C(A\upharpoonright n|D\upharpoonright n)=C(D\upharpoonright n|A\upharpoonright n)=O(1)$;
 \item[(2)] For all $x$, there is a random $z$ such that $z \geq_{rK} x$ (or $z \geq_K x$).
 \end{enumerate} (Verbatim from the paper's TeX; symbols are the source paper's. Stated as open/conjectural; no resolution of it was found in the paper's own text by the rules of problem_index.py - a paper may still prove special cases of a conjecture it states.)

