[Lem Kac mom of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] {Kajino_Noda_26_Kac}}]  
  Let $A=(A_{t})_{t \geq 0}$ be a PCAF and let $\nu$ be the associated smooth measure.
  Then, for any $t \in (0,\infty)$, $x \in M$, and $n \in \mathbb{N}$,
  \begin{equation}
    E_x[A_t^n] 
    =n!\int_{\{0 < t_1 < \cdots < t_n \leq t\}} \int_{M^n}
    \prod_{j=1}^n p_{t_j -t_{j-1}}(x_{j-1},x_j)\, \nu(dx_1)\cdots\nu(dx_n)\,dt_1\cdots dt_n,
  \end{equation}
  where we set $x_0 \coloneqq x$ and $t_0 \coloneqq 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary propTW of arXiv:2607.14792, 'On the degree distribution of large tentacular Bienaymé--Galton--Watson trees'] Let $\mu$ be an offspring distribution and $T_n^{k_n}$ a $\mu$-BGW tree conditioned to have $n$ vertices and $k_n$ leaves. Then, we have the following equality
\begin{equation*}
 \mathbb{P}\left(T \in \mathbb{T}^{k_n}_{n}\right) = \frac{1}{n}\mathbb{P}\left(B_{n}=k_n\right)\mathbb{P}\left(W'_{n-k_n} = k_n-1\right),   
\end{equation*}
where $B_{n}$ is the sum of $n$ independent Bernoulli random variables with parameter $\mu(0)$ and  $W'$ the random walk started from $W'_0=0$ with step distribution $\xi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Dfn 73 (Annealed AP entropy) of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Let $\phi \in \B(\A,\rmM_k)_+$. Its \textbf{annealed almost periodic} (`\textbf{AP}') \textbf{entropy along $\bspi$} is the quantity
\begin{equation}
\rmh^\ann_{\bspi}(\phi) := \inf_O \limsup_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{d_n}\log \bbE\frac{\vol_{2kd_n}\X(\pi_n,O)}{v(d_n)^k},
\end{equation}
where the infimum runs over all neighbourhoods of $\phi$.

Similarly, the \textbf{lower AP entropy of $\phi$ along $\bspi$} is the quantity
\begin{equation}
\ul{\rmh}^\ann_{\bspi}(\phi) := \inf_O \liminf_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{d_n}\log \bbE\frac{\vol_{2kd_n}\X(\pi_n,O)}{v(d_n)^k},
\end{equation}
where the infimum runs over all neighbourhoods of $\phi$.

[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] There exists a positive constant $\uc{c:approximation}>0$ such that, for every $r \geq 2$, $x \in \Z^{2}$, and $t \geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
\P \big( |g_{x}-g_{x}^{r}| \geq t \big) \leq 2e^{-\uc{c:approximation}t^{2}r^{2\beta-2}}.
\end{equation}

