[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Suppose $0 \leq \chi < 1$ and $u_0$ satisfies the conditions of \Cref{main_result_theorem}. Then there exists positive constants $C$ and $T$ so that
        for all $t > 0$,
        \begin{equation}
            u\left(t, x + 2t - \frac{3}{2}\log t\right) \leq \begin{cases}
                CU_*(x) + \frac{C}{(t+T)^{1-\eta}} & x \leq B\\
                CU_*(x) + \frac{C}{t^{1-\eta}}e^{-(1-\eta)x} & B \leq x \leq \log(t + T) + \frac{3}{2}\log(t) +B\\
                C\left(x- \frac{3}{2}\log t\right)e^{-x}e^{- \frac{\left(x-\frac{3}{2}\log t - B\right)^2}{4(t+T)}} & x \geq \log(t + T) + \frac{3}{2}\log(t) + B,
            \end{cases}
        \end{equation}
        with $B := 2T + L_0 + L_1$ and $\eta > 0$ that can be chosen arbitrarily small. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 12 ($\hat\bS_\up{\alpha,\nu}(\cU_-)\subseteq\cD_0$ for general measures) of arXiv:2606.27774, 'Variational Formulas for the Spectrum of\\ Block Wishart Matrices'] Let $\alpha \in (0,\infty)$.
Assume $\nu \in\cuP_0(\sa{k}{\C})$ (i.e., $\nu$ is a compactly supported measure).
Then for any $\bU \in\cU_-$, we have 
\begin{equation}
    \hat\bS_\up{\alpha,\nu}(\bU) \in \cD_0.
\end{equation}

