body:
[Lemma 7 (Mellin quotient and uniqueness) of arXiv:2606.18458, 'Stable size-biasing and the positive scale-mixture order of generalized Gaussian laws'] Let $p,q>0$. If $V>0$, $V\perp X_q$, and $X_p\stackrel{d}{=}VX_q$, then, for every $t\in\R$,
\begin{equation}
\E V^{it}=\frac{2^{it/p}\Gamma((1+it)/p)\Gamma(1/q)}{2^{it/q}\Gamma((1+it)/q)\Gamma(1/p)}=:\Phi_{p,q}(t).

\end{equation}
Consequently, whenever a strictly positive independent factor exists, its law is unique.

[Prop Laplacian-approximation-local of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Consider an s-embedding $\mathcal{S}^{(t)}(\Lambda_{n})$ constructed by Lemma (lem:SDE-embedding of the paper) and a real function $\phi$. Then, with $\mathbf{P}$-probability at least $1-O(n^{-4})$, there exist a constant $O=O(\omega,\alpha)>0$ such that for any $0\leq t \leq t^{(\alpha)}_n$,
\begin{equation}
		[\Delta_{\mathcal{S}^{(t)}}\phi](v)= \pm_{v} \delta \big[ \Delta\phi + O(\delta^{1+\alpha} \sup|D^{(2)}\phi| ) + O(\delta^{2+\alpha} \sup|D^{(3)}\phi |) \big],
\end{equation}
where the supremum are taken in a disc of size $10\delta$ around $v$.

