[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] For any $f\in L^1(\R^d)$ with $f\ge 0$ and $\epsilon>0$, we have
		\begin{align*}
			\mathcal{R}^X_{f_\epsilon}(t)\le \mathcal{R}^X_f(t)
		\end{align*}
		for all $t\ge 0$,
		where $f_\epsilon = f\ast \rho_\epsilon$.

