[Prop Splev-cc of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The global $\infty$-category ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}$ is globally presentable.
    \begin{proof}
        We begin by proving that ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}$ is fiberwise presentable. For this we note once more that if $G$ is any compact Lie group, then ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})$ is presentable by Proposition~(prop:mySplev-unpar-presh of the paper). Let now $V$ be any $H$-representation; by the previous lemma $\ev_V\colon{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})\to{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{\textup{$(G\times H)$-gl},*}$ is cocontinuous. Thus, in the naturality square
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                {\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G'})\arrow[d,"\ev_V"']\arrow[r,"f^*"] & {\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})\arrow[d,"\ev_V"]\\
                {{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{\text{$(G'\times H)$-gl},*}\arrow[r,"f^*"'] & {{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{\text{$(G\times H)$-gl},*} 
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        all maps except possibly the top one preserve colimits. As for varying $V$ the right-hand vertical maps are jointly conservative, also $f^*\colon{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G'})\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})$ is cocontinuous, hence a left adjoint by the Adjoint Functor Theorem.

        Next, we recall once more that each $f^*\colon{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G}')\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})$ admits a left adjoint $\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!$, whence so does more generally any restriction along a map $f\colon X\to\mathbb B{G}$ in $\PSh(\textup{Glo})$ by Remark~(rk:cleft-cc-addendum of the paper). It remains to verify the Beck--Chevalley conditions from Lemma~(lemma:S-cocompleteness-repr of the paper), i.e.\ that for any pullback
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                X'\arrow[r, "f'"]\arrow[d, "g'"']\arrow[dr,pullback] & \mathbb B{H}\arrow[d, "g"]\\
                X\arrow[r, "f"'] & \mathbb B{G}
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        in $\PSh(\textup{Glo})$ the Beck--Chevalley map $\textup{BC}_!\colon\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!'g'^*\to g^*\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!
        $ is invertible. By Lemma~(lemma:ev-V-jointly-repr of the paper) the functors $\ev_V$ are jointly conservative, so it will suffice to show that the Beck--Chevalley map is an equivalence after hitting it with $\ev_V$ for every representation $V$. But we have a commutative diagram of Beck--Chevalley maps
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                \ev_V\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!'g'^*\arrow[r,"\textup{BC}_!"]\arrow[d,"\ev_V\textup{BC}_!"'] & \textbf{\textup{L}}f_!'\ev_Vg'^*\arrow[r,"\sim"] & \textbf{\textup{L}}f'_!g'^*\ev_V\arrow[d,"\textup{BC}_!"]\\
                \ev_Vg^*\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!\arrow[r,"\sim"'] & \ev_Vg^*\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!\arrow[r,"g^*\textup{BC}_!"'] & g^*\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!\ev_V
            \end{tikzcd} 
        \]
        in which the two horizontal Beck--Chevalley maps are equivalences as $\ev_V$ is a left adjoint, while the right-hand vertical map i (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition eq:cf_tempered of arXiv:2412.06374, 'Stable and tempered stable distributions and processes: an overview toward trajectory simu'] Let $(X_t)_{t\in \mathbb{R}}$ be a CTS Lévy process with Lévy triplet $\left(b_\nu, 0,\nu\right)$ where $\nu$ defined as in (equation eq:levy_measure_tempered_stable of the paper) and $b_\nu=\int_{|x|>1}x \nu(dx)$. For $t\in \mathbb{R}_+$, the characteristic function exponent can be expressed for $u\in \mathbb{R}$ as 
\begin{align}
\log(\phi_{X_t}(u))= \begin{cases} 
tP\Gamma(-\alpha)\left((A-iu)^\alpha - A^\alpha + iu\alpha A^{\alpha-1} \right) + tQ\Gamma(-\alpha)\left((B+iu)^\alpha - B^\alpha + iu\alpha B^{\alpha-1}  \right) & \alpha \neq 1,\\
iut(P-Q) + tP(A-iu)\log\left(1-\frac{iu}{A}\right) + tQ(B-iu)\log\left(1-\frac{iu}{B}\right)& \alpha = 1.
\end{cases}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:covreperror of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] Assume the system properties described by (equation eq:realhidden of the paper) for the true hidden state, (equation eq:asshidden of the paper) for the assumed hidden state and (equation eq:obs of the paper) for the observation model.  Given $r,s$ such that $r <s, r >0$, we have the following evolution equations for the  error covariance $P_t$ and expected squared error $\tilde{P}_t$,
\begin{align}

	\frac{dP_t}{dt} &= (G -(r-s)K_tH) P_t  + P_t (G -(r-s)K_tH)^\top  + \Sigma   + (r-s)^2 K_t \Xi K_t^\top   \\

	\frac{d\tilde{P}_t}{dt} &= (G -(r-s)K_tH)\tilde{P}_t  + \tilde{P}_t(G -(r-s)K_tH)^\top  + \Sigma  + (r-s)^2 K_t \Xi K_t^\top   - \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_t]b^\top  - b \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_t^\top]  
\end{align}
where $K_t$ is the continuous time Kalman gain matrix as defined in (equation eq:kalmangain of the paper).  For the special case $s=0,r=1$, it holds that $P_t = C_t, \enskip \forall \enskip t > 0$ if $P_0 = C_0$ where $C_t$ is the solution of the covariance equation of the replicator-mutator.\\
\\
Furthermore, for any p.d. $C_0$,  the evolution of the mean squared error $E_t$ satisfies the following inequality 
\begin{align}


	\frac{dE_t}{dt} \leq \alpha(A_t(r,s) + A_t(r,s)^\top)E_t - 2\text{Tr}[\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_t]b^\top] + \text{Tr}[\Sigma] + (r-s)^2 \alpha(H^\top \Xi^{-1}H) \|C_t\|_F
\end{align}
where $A_t$ is defined in (equation eq:defnAt of the paper) and $\alpha(A)$ denotes the largest eigenvalue of $A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

