	for all $N\geq 1$. Assume \eqref{c1}. Then, for every $Y\in L^2(\Omega)$,
	\begin{equation*}
		(X_N, Y) \xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{(d)} (Z, Y),
	\end{equation*}
	where $Z\sim N(0,\sigma^2)$ and $Z$, $Y$ are independent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:p-moment estimate of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Suppose Assumption (asp:potential of the paper) holds. For any $p\geq 2$ and $\xi\in L^p(\Omega,\mathcal F_0,\mathbf P)$, there exists $C(p)=C(p,\alpha,\beta,\delta,\overline{\sigma}, L)>0$ such that the unique solution $\{X_t^{\xi}\}_{t\geq 0}$ of (equation eq:mvsystem of the paper) satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{E}[|X_t^{\xi}|^p]\leq e^{-pt}\mathbf{E}[|\xi|^p]+C(p), \ \text{ for all } \ t\geq 0.
    \end{equation}

