body:
[Theorem thm:PoC of arXiv:2602.00988, 'Wealth exchange under ceiling and flooring constraints: a modified Bennati–Dragulescu–Yako'] Assume that ${\bf p}(t)=\{p_n(t)\}_{n\geq 0}$ is a classical solution of
(equation eq:law_limit of the paper)-(equation eq:two-classes of the paper) such that ${\bf p}(0) \in
\mathcal{P}(\mathbb N)$ with mean $\mu \in \mathbb N_+$, and ${\bf p}_{\mathrm{emp}}(t)$
represents the empirical distribution associated to the modified BDY model
(equation dynamics:modified_BDY of the paper). Then there exists some universal constant
$C > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bf p}(t) - {\bf p}_{\mathrm{emp}}(t)\|_{\ell^1}\right] \leq \left[\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bf p}(0) - {\bf p}_{\mathrm{emp}}(0)\|_{\ell^1}\right] + \frac{C\,t\,\sqrt{\log N}}{\sqrt{N}}\right]\,\mathrm{e}^{8t}
\end{equation}
for all $t\geq 0$. In particular, if $\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bf p}(0) - {\bf p}_{\mathrm{emp}}(0)\|_{\ell^1}\right] \xrightarrow{N \to 0} 0$, then for any $T > 0$, $\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bf p}(t) - {\bf p}_{\mathrm{emp}}(t)\|_{\ell^1}\right] \xrightarrow{N \to 0} 0$ for each $t\in [0,T]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

