body:
[Lemma 1BE of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Consider a local function $f:\Omega\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ whose support is included in~$\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0-1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$. There exists a constant $C_{13}=C_{13}(\kappa ,\rho ,\mathcal{E} ,f)>0$ such that for any $t\in [0,T]$ and any measurable function $v:[0,T]\longrightarrow\ell^2(\mathbb{Z} )$, we have 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}\left[\left(\int_0^t \sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}}\tau_x \big\{ f(s) - \mathbb{E}_{\ell_0}[f](s)\big\} v_s(x)\,\mathrm{d} s\right)^2\right] \le C_{13}\frac{\ell_0^3}{N^a}\int_0^t \| v_s\|^2\,\mathrm{d} s.
    \end{equation}

