[Theorem thm:existence_all_cases of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] Assume that Assumptions (assu:space of the paper) and (assu:noise of the paper) are satisfied. Then, for any $p\ge 2$ and for any initial datum $u(0)\in L^p(\Omega,\mathcal{F}_0,\mathbb{P};H)$, there exists a unique $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. continuous and adapted
strong solution $u(t)$, $t\in [0,T]$ of (equation eq:gen_model of the paper), and there exists a constant $C_{p,T}>0$, such that
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}(\|u(t)\|^p)\leq C_{p,T}\left(1+\mathbb{E}\|u(0)\|^p\right),\quad t\in[0,T].
\end{align*}

[Corollary 9 (Application to light tails -- random thresholds) of arXiv:2506.20789, 'Central limit theory for Peaks-over-Threshold partial sums of long memory linear time seri'] Under the Assumptions of Corollary~\ref{cor:light_det} and with the notation of Corollary~\ref{cor:heavy_rand} it holds, as $n\to\infty$,
 \begin{align*}
  &
    n^{1/2-d}
    \left(
    q_{X_0}
    \left(
    1
    -
    \frac{k}{n}
    \right)
    \right)^{1-\beta}
    \\&
    \cdot
    \
      \left(
      \frac
      {
      \sum_{i=1}^{k}
        \log(
        X_{n-i+1:n}
        /
        X_{n-k:n}
        )
      }
      {n \PP[X_0>u_n]}
      \ - \
      \EE[\log(X_0/u_n) \mid X_0>u_n]
      \right)
