[Theorem thm:theStableManifold of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $\alpha =1$,  $g$ be sufficiently small and $L$ be sufficiently large.

Then there exist convergent sequences 
\begin{align}
	( \textbf{a}^{(\emptyset)}_{c,k} ,  \nu^{(\emptyset)}_{c,k} )_{k \in \N \cup \{\infty\}} \subset  \operatorname{HB}_{\epsilon_p} \times \R
\end{align}
such that $\textbf{a}_{c,\infty}^{(\emptyset)} =0$ and satisfies the following stability condition:
whenever $\vec{\nu}, \vec{\textbf{a}} \in \R^{\kA_0 \cup \kA_1}$ are given by
\begin{align}
\begin{cases}
	\nu^{(\emptyset)} =  \nu_{c,k}^{(\emptyset)}  \text{ and } \nu^{(\km)} = - \textbf{a}_{c,k}^{(\km)} \text{ for each } \km \in \kA_1 \\
	\vec{\textbf{a}} = \vec{\textbf{a}}_{c,k}
\end{cases}
\end{align}
the bulk RG flow of infinite length exists with $\vec{\textbf{a}}$ and initial condition
\begin{align}
	\vec{\nu}_0 = \vec{\nu},  \quad g^{(\emptyset)}_0 = g,  \quad g^{(\km_2)} =0 \;\; (\km_2 \in \ko_{4,\nabla}),  \quad K_0 \equiv 0 .
\end{align}
Moreover,  $\nu^{(\emptyset)}_{c,\infty},  \textbf{a}^{(\km)}_{c,\infty} = O(g)$ for each $\km \in \kA_1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

