[Cor EL_gauge_cor of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $R\subset \mathbb{R}^d$ and a suitable boundary function $H_b$ on $\partial R$. If $H$ is a weak solution to the differential equation 
    \begin{align}
         \text{div} (\nabla F(\nabla H)) = 0
    \end{align}
    with $H\mid_{\partial R} = H_b$, the limiting gauge flow is $\alpha = \nabla H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:basic-facts-no-assumptions of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ be a gamble space and $X,Y:\Omega\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ variables.
  Then we have
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item $\overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} (X + c) = \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X + c$ for all $c\in\mathbb{R}$ (translation)
  \item $X \leq Y \implies \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X \leq \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} Y$ (monotonicity).
  \end{enumerate}

