so, $\Phi_{t+s}=\Phi_{t}\circ\Phi_s$ which implies that $\{\Phi_t\}_{t\geq 0}$ is a semi-group of mappings on","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:a0998432598f8e334068b5bc522c28d9303a3b606270e4363c36d894153be616","revision_digest":"sha256:9dcdc49d5b6ff22655d8d4caafde7d2ee9a110aff59a2e7be2e34360c891a5b4","source_id":"arxiv:2506.13347","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

