body:
[Corollary cor:ordinary-lumped-BE-kernel of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] Let $\overline K_{\mathrm{BE}}$ and $\overline\pi_{\mathrm{BE}}$ be the transition kernel and stationary distribution of the lumped Bose--Einstein Markov chain on $\mathrm{Comp}_{n,k}$. Then for all $\bm{i},\bm{j}\in\mathrm{Comp}_{n,k}$,
\begin{equation}
 \overline K_{\mathrm{BE}}(\bm{i},\bm{j})
 =
 \sum_{M=(m_{a,b})\in\mathcal{M}(\bm{i},\bm{j})}
 \prod_{a,b=1}^k
 \frac{(1/k)_{(m_{a,b})}}{m_{a,b}!},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \overline\pi_{\mathrm{BE}}(\bm{i})
 =
 \frac1{\binom{n+k-1}{k-1}}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma l:intermediate_estimate_pressure_deterministic0 of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (t:caccioppoli of the paper), for all $\alpha\in (0,1)$,  it holds that  
\begin{align*}
\Big({\mathbf E}\sup_{\alpha I}\Big\|v-\fint_{\alpha B} v\Big\|_{L^2(\alpha B)}^r\Big)^{1/r}
&+
\big({\mathbf E}\|\nabla v\|_{L^2(\alpha Q)}^r\big)^{1/r}\\
&+
\big({\mathbf E}\|(\nabla \widetilde{\pi}_n)_n\|_{L^{2}(\alpha Q;\ell^2)}^r\big)^{1/r}
\leq C_0 \mathcal{E}_{Q}^{\#} ,
\end{align*}
where $C_0$ depends only on $d,M,\varrho,\nu,\nu_0,r$ and $\alpha$ and $\mathcal{E}_Q^{\#}$ is as in (equation eq:def_En_Q_caccioppoli of the paper).

