[Prop geographic ineq decoupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $u\in \widetilde{\mathcal{W}}_n$ be such that $|u|_\gamma\leqslant (\lambda_\gamma+\varepsilon) n$ for $\gamma\in \{1,2\}$ and set $(u^1,\ldots, u^r)=F_{n}(u)$. For $\gamma\in \{1,2\}$, we denote by $\underline v^{(\gamma)}$ the list $ (u^{j_\gamma(1)},\ldots, u^{j_\gamma(r_\gamma)})$. 
	Assume that $\underline v^{(\gamma)}\neq(e,\ldots,e)$ for $\gamma\in \{1,2\}$.
	Then, for all $w\in \Phi_n(u)$, 
	\begin{equation}

		d_{\mathrm{LP}}(L^{(\gamma)}[u],L[w])\leqslant  h\Big(\frac {{|\underline v^{(\gamma)}|}}{|u|_\gamma}\Big)+2h\Big(\frac{|\underline v^{(\gamma)}|}{T_\gamma}\Big).
	\end{equation}

