[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] There exists a sequence $(x_N,y_N)_{N\in\N}$ such that
\begin{gather}
    \liminf_{N\to\infty}A_N(x_N,y_N)\leq \liminf_{N\to\infty}\E_{x,y} A_N(x,y), \\
    \lim_{N\to\infty}\Delta_N(x_N,y_N)=0, \\
    \lim_{N\to\infty} \mcl D_N(x_N,y_N) = 0. 
\end{gather}
There also exists another sequence $(x'_N,y'_N)_{N\in\N}$ such that
\begin{align}
     \limsup_{N\to\infty}\E_{x,y} A_N(x,y)\leq \limsup_{N\to\infty}A_N(x'_N,y'_N), 
\end{align}
and such that~\eqref{e.limDelta_N(x_N)=02} and~\eqref{e.lim|dF^x=dF^x|=02} hold with $(x'_N,y'_N)$ in place of $(x_N,y_N)$.

