body:
[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2607.07022, 'Coordinate-wise Elephant Random Walk'] There exists $C_f<\infty$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \left |\Var(f(S_{t+1}) \mid \F_t)-v_f(S_t) \right| \leq C_f \max_{1 \leq i \leq k} |\widehat{m}_t^{(i)}|, \quad t \ge 0 , 
    \end{equation*}
    where $\widehat{m}_t^{(i)}$ is the memory bias defined in \eqref{eq:mhat}. In particular, if $\max_{1\le i \le k} p_i<1$, then the conditional variance is approximated by $v_f$ in \eqref{eq:vfx}: 
    \begin{equation*}
        \left |\Var(f(S_{t+1}) \mid \F_t)-v_f(S_t) \right| \xrightarrow[t\to \infty]{a.s} 0 . 
    \end{equation*}

