[Proposition prop:exp_est of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] Let $\phi$ be a solution of (equation eq:main of the paper) in the sense of (def-sol-H1 of the paper), then the following exponential bound holds
    \begin{align*}
    \mathbb{P}\left( \sup_{t\ge 0} \left(\|\phi(t)\|_V^2 - \|\phi_0\|_V^2 + \frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \|\phi(s)\|_W^2 ds - \kappa t \right) \ge R\right) \le e^{-\frac{R}{2C\kappa}},
\end{align*}

