[Theorem 29 of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] Let $A,~ B \in  \mathcal{M}_{n}(\mathbb{R})$  be symmetric and let $S \in  M_{n,m}$. Then

\begin{enumerate}
\item  if $A \geqm B$, then $S^\top AS \geqm  S^\top BS$;
\item  if $\rank S = m$, then $A \gm B$ implies $S^\top AS \gm  S^\top BS$
\item if $m = n$ and $S \in M_n$ is nonsingular, then $A \gm B $ if and only if $S^\top AS \gm  S^\top BS$;
									$A \geqm B $  if and only if $S^\top AS \geqm  S^\top BS$;
\item  $I_m \gm S^\top S$ (respectively, $I_n\gm SS^\top$) if and only if $S$ is a strict contraction; $I_m \geqm S^\top S$ (respectively, $I_n\geqm SS^\top$) if and only if $S$ is a  contraction;

										\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 3 (Exact trace identity) of arXiv:2608.27657, '\bfseries Stein Kernels and Normal Approximation\\ for Log-Concave Bilinear Forms'] In the regular moment-map model, suppose that
\(\E\Tr(H^2)<\infty\).  Then
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \Var(f_A)=\Var(q_A)-3T_A+U_A.}
  \tag{3.4}
\end{equation}

