[Lemma 83 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] There exist a constant $C > 0$ and a function $c\,:\,\amsmathbb{R}_{> 0} \rightarrow \amsmathbb{R}_{> 0}$ such that, for any $h \in [H]$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\forall z \in \amsmathbb{M}_h \quad \big|\phi^{\pm}_h(z)\big| \leq C$;
\item for $\eta > 0$ small enough and $x \in [\hat{a}'_{h} + \eta,\hat{b}'_{h} - \eta]$ we have $|\phi_h^{\pm}(x)| \geq c(\eta)$;
\item if $\iota_h^->0$, then $\phi_h^-(\hat{a}'_{h}) = 0$; if $\iota_h^+>0$, then $\phi_h^+(\hat{b}'_{h}) = 0$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem l.version of arXiv:2507.16056, 'Conditional GMC within the stochastic heat flow'] For every deterministic $g,g'\inL^2(\mathbb{R}^4,\mathrm{d} x)$ and $a<\infty$,
\begin{align}

	\int_{\Gamma_0^2} 
	\mathbf{E}(M_{0} + M_{0'})^{\otimes 2}(\mathrm{d}\gamma, \mathrm{d}\eta)
	\, |g(\gamma(s),\eta(s))\,g'(\gamma(t),\eta(t))| 
	\,
	e^{a\tau_0(\gamma,\eta)} 
	<
	\infty\ .
\end{align}

