[Lemma eq:rep of arXiv:2508.09291, '1+O(1) asymptotics for loop percolation in five and higher dimensions'] Write $K\xleftrightarrow{\,\,{\omega}\,\,}L$ if $\omega$ intersects both $K,L\subset\mathbb{Z}^d$. If $K$ and $L$ are two finite disjoint sets, then
    \begin{equation}
        \mu\ek{\omega\colon K\xleftrightarrow{\,\,{\omega}\,\,}L}=\sum_{x\in K}\sum_{m\ge 1}\frac{1}{m}\mathbb{P}_x\rk{\omega\rk{\tau_{2m}}=x}\, ,
    \end{equation}
    where $\tau_0=0$, $\tau_{2m+1}=\inf\gk{t>\tau_{2m}\colon \omega(t)\in L}$ and $\tau_{2m+2}=\inf\gk{t>\tau_{2m+1}\colon \omega(t)\in K}$, $m\ge 0$. Furthermore,
    \begin{equation}
        \mu\ek{\#{\mathcal R }(\omega)\textnormal{ with } K\xleftrightarrow{\,\,{\omega}\,\,}L}=\sum_{x\in K}\sum_{m\ge 1}\frac{1}{m}\mathbb{E}_x\ek{\#{\mathcal R }\rk{\omega\rk{\tau_{2m}}},\, \omega\rk{\tau_{2m}}=x}\, .
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem Thm TVS Ising of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Let $D$ be a simply connected domain and $z_1 \neq z_2 \in D$. Let $E^{\rm Ising}_{\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2}$ 
denote the event that one of the CLE$_4$ gaskets obtained from the following iteration comes $\varepsilon_1$-close to $z_1$ and $\varepsilon_2$-close to $z_2$.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item We sample a CLE$_4$ gasket in $D$ to obtain $A_1$; 
\item Inside each connected component of $D \setminus A_1$, we sample a random gasket with the law of the two-valued set $A_{-2\sqrt{2}\lambda + 2\lambda, 2\lambda}$ to obtain $A_2$;
\item we then again sample CLE$_4$ inside each connected component of $A_2$ and iterate this way: on odd steps we sample CLE$_4$ gaskets, on even $A_{-2\sqrt{2}\lambda + 2\lambda, 2\lambda}$ gaskets.
\end{enumerate}
Then the Ising spin two-point function in the unit disk is given by 
$$\lim_{\max(\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2) \to 0} (\varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2)^{-1/8}
\mathbb{P}(E^{\rm Ising}_{\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2}) = C_2\CR(z_1,D)^{-1/8}\CR(z_2,D)^{-1/8}\frac{\theta_3(q^{1/4})}{\theta_2(q^{1/4})},$$
where $C_2$ is an absolute constant, and the nome $q$ is fixed by $\exp(\pi G_D(z_1,z_2)) = \frac{\theta_3(q^{1/2})}{\theta_2(q^{1/2})}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:caterpillar_bound of arXiv:2604.09509, 'An Improved Bipartition Cover Bound for the Multispecies Coalescent Model'] Suppose $h: \mathbb{N} \to [0,1]$ is a decreasing function and $\mathbb{P}(E_{i,1}) \geqslant h(k_i)$. If we have a species tree with $k$ species and a set $\cG$ of at least

\begin{equation}
    n_h := \inf\left\{n \in \mathbb{N} : \sum_{\ell=2}^{k-2}\left[1-h(\ell)\right]^n \leqslant 1-q\right\}
\end{equation}

\noindent gene trees sampled independently under the MSC model, then $\cG$ forms a bipartition cover of the species tree with probability at least $q$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

