[Theorem thm:harmonizable of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Let $\widetilde{M}_\alpha$ be a complex isotropic S$\alpha$S random
measure on $\mathbb{R}$ with Lebesgue control measure. Under
Assumption~(ass:params of the paper), define
\begin{equation}

\widetilde{X}^{(n)}_H(t)
:= \mathrm{Re}\int_\mathbb{R}
\frac{\Gamma(1/\alpha)}{\alpha\sqrt{2\pi}}\cdot
\frac{e^{it\xi}
  - \displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\frac{(it\xi)^k}{k!}}
{|\xi|^{H(t)+1/\alpha}}\,
e^{-i\pi(1-1/\alpha)\,\mathrm{sign}(\xi)/2}
\,d\widetilde{M}_\alpha(\xi).
\end{equation}
Then $\{X^{(n)}_H(t)\}_{t\in\mathbb{R}}$ and
$\{\widetilde{X}^{(n)}_H(t)\}_{t\in\mathbb{R}}$ have identical
finite-dimensional distributions. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem.dpiconstant of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Suppose that $p > 4$, $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$ is any probability space, $t_0 \in [0,1)$, $X_0 \in L^p(\Omega)$, $\widebar\alpha \in L^{\infty}(\Omega)$ with $\|\widebar\alpha\|_2 \leq c_0$, and $h \in (0,1-t_0)$. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{V}_p^+\big( t_0, \mathcal{L}(X_0) \big) \leq \mathcal{V}_p^+\big( t_0 + h, \mathcal{L}(X_0 + h \widebar\alpha) * \gamma_h \big).
    \end{align*}

