[Theorem 9 (Non-critical power-rate estimate) of arXiv:2608.17540, 'Pathwise stability for one-dimensional SDEs driven by Brownian motion and a symmetric stab'] Assume Assumptions~\ref{ass:baseline}--\ref{ass:solutions}. Suppose $B,A,S<1$.
If $\wt\eta\in(1/\alpha,1]$, then there exists $C>0$ such that
\begin{align}
\sup_{0\le t\le T}\E|X_t-\wt X_t|^{\alpha-1}
\le C\Bigg[&|x_0-\wt x_0|^{\alpha-1} \notag\\
&+\max\left\{
B^{\frac{\alpha\wt\eta-1}{\alpha\wt\eta-\alpha+1}},
A^{\frac{2(\alpha\wt\eta-1)}{\alpha\wt\eta-\alpha+2}},
S^{\alpha-1/\wt\eta}
\right\}\Bigg]. 
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem : LDP/ContinuousMetric/LDP of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] The process $(\TightSPT)_{n\ge 1}$ follows the LDP with the good rate function
	\begin{align}
		\FdT^{(b)} : \mathcal F_{\mathrm b}  &\longrightarrow \intervalleff0\infty \eol
			D &\longmapsto \begin{cases} \infty \quad &\text{if } D\notin \RegPD[\mu^{(b)}], \\ \FdT^{-, (b)}(D) \quad &\text{if } D\in \RegPD[\mu^{(b)}]. \end{cases}
	\end{align}

