[Corollary 13 (Quadratic-moment form bound) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There is $C_U(\gamma,Q)<\infty$ such that, on the closed form domain,
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\C}|x|^2f^2\,\D\nu
 \le C_U(\gamma,Q)\left(\int_{\C}|\nabla f|^2\,\D\nu+\int_{\C} f^2\,\D\nu\right).
\end{equation}

