[Lemma l-jl of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Let $X$ be a non-negative random variable. Then,
\begin{equation*}
E[X^a] \,\le\,  E[X]^{\theta/c}\, E[X^b]^{(1-\theta)/c}
\end{equation*}
for all $a>0$, $b>0$ and $0<\theta<1$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\theta \,+\, (1-\theta) b \,>\, a\;.
\end{equation*}
In this formula $c = [\, \theta \,+\, (1-\theta) b\,]/ a >1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:dc-clean-scalar-trace-defect of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] If $C_1(u)+\Lambda_2(u)C_2(u)^{-1}=a(u)I$ for a scalar
function~$a$, then
\begin{align}
\frac{
\left(D_1-a(u)D_2-\frac{1}{2}D_2^2\right)
F(S_3u)\cdot F(u)
}{
F(S_3u)F(u)
}
&=
\frac{1}{2}
\left[
\operatorname{tr}_E\bigl(\mathcal B(u)^2\bigr)
-
\bigl(\operatorname{tr}_E\mathcal B(u)\bigr)^2
\right].

\end{align}
When $\dim E = 1$, the trace-defect term vanishes and the
Fredholm determinant satisfies the scalar Hirota equation
\begin{equation}
\left(D_1-a(u)D_2-\frac{1}{2}D_2^2\right)
F(S_3u)\cdot F(u) = 0.
\end{equation}

