[Lemma Phi-equicont of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Fix $0<\delta <\eta <1$ and $i\in \{1,2\}$. Then there
exists $N$ such that for all $n\geq N$ and all $x,y\in \lbrack \delta ,\eta
] $, 
\begin{equation}
|\Phi _{n}^{i}(x)-\Phi _{n}^{i}(y)|\leq |x-y|.  
