[Proposition prop:upper of arXiv:2606.11248, 'Persistent Homology of the Planar Wiener Sausage: Brownian Scaling and a Logarithmic Expec'] There exists an absolute constant $c_{+}<\infty$ such that, for every fixed $r>0$,
\begin{equation}
\limsup_{T\to\infty}\frac{(\log T)^{2}}{T}\,\mathbb{E}[\beta_{1}^{T}(r)]\le\frac{c_{+}}{r^{2}}.
\end{equation}

