body:
[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2506.17470, 'The coalescent of a sample from a linear-fractional branching process'] Let  $\mathbf{T}_k$ be a $k$-sample tree. For any $x_1,\dots, x_{k-1} \in  \{1,\ldots, T\}$, let $\{y_1,\ldots, y_d\}$ be the set of its different values, $d< k$. Then, for any $m\ge 0$, 
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{P}(N_T=m+k, H_{k,0}=T, H_{k,1}\leq x_1, \dots, H_{k,k-1}\leq x_{k-1})\\
 &\hspace{2.5cm}=
{ k+m \choose k }^{-1} \left( \underset{j=1}{\overset{d}{\prod}}p_j^{r_j}\right)(1-p_0)
 \underset{j=1}{\overset{d}{\sum}} 
 \frac{ p_j^{d-2}(p_j^{m+2}-p_0^{m+2})}{(p_j-p_0)\underset{i=1,i\neq j}{\overset{d}{\prod}}(p_j-p_i)},
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
where $p_0=\mathbb{P}(H\leq T)$, $p_j=\mathbb{P}(H \leq y_j)$ and $r_j=\#\{i <k: x_i=y_j\}$  for $j=1,\ldots,d$.

