[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Let~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ have the law of $\{\frac12|B_k|^2\}_{k\ge0}$ for~$B$ denoting a standard two-dimen\-sional Brownian motion. Let~$\{Z_{T_k}\}_{k\ge0}$  be a sequence of random Borel measures on~$[0,1]$ coupled with~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ so that \eqref{E:1.21a} holds as stated. Then
\begin{equation}

\ZZ(\textd x)\laweq \sum_{k\ge1}1_{ [b^{-k-1},b^{-k})}(x)\, b^{-2k} Z_{T_k}\bigl(b^k\textd x\bigr). 
\end{equation}
A.e.\ sample of~$\ZZ$ is diffuse. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

