[Lemma 49 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For each $t \in [0,T]$ the set $\bbb_t$ endowed with the metric
\begin{align*}
d \big( (Y,Y'), (Z,Z') \big) := \| (Y,Y') - (Z,Z') \|_{X,2\alpha;[0,t]}, \quad (Y,Y'), (Z,Z') \in \bbb_t
\end{align*}
is a complete metric space.

