body:
[Lemma lem:interpolation of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $p\in[1,\infty)$, $k,\ell\in\mathbb{N}$, $k$ even. Take a  linear map $T:\mathcal{C}^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)\mapsto L^p(\Omega)$ such there exist positive constants $\Gamma_{\ell}\leq\Gamma_{-k}$ so that the following holds: for any $f\in \mathcal{C}^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)$ the following bounds hold                       

    \begin{equs}
       \|Tf\|_{L^p(\Omega)} &\leq \Gamma_{\ell}\|\nabla^\ell f\|_{\infty},\\
        \|T(\nabla^k f)\|_{L^p(\Omega)} &\leq \Gamma_{-k}\|f\|_{\infty}.  
    \end{equs}
    Suppose furthermore that $Tf_n\to T f$ in $L^p(\Omega)$ whenever $f_n\to f$ uniformly on compacts.
    Then for any $\beta\in[-k,0)$ there exists a constant $C=C(d,\ell,k,\beta)$ such that for all $f\in \mathcal{C}^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)$ one has
    \begin{equ}
          \|Tf\|_{L^p(\Omega)} \leq C \Gamma_{\ell}^{1-\theta}\Gamma_{-k}^{\theta}\|f\|_{\mathcal{C}^{{\beta}}},   
    \end{equ}
    where $\theta\in[0,1]$ is uniquely defined by $\beta=(1-\theta)\ell-\theta k$.

