[Thm 1 (Theorem \ref{Thm psi GMC}) of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $n\geq 1$.
Then the field $\psi_{n,A}$ is the limit, as $\gamma\to 0^{+}$,
of the following continuous function supported of $D\setminus A$:
\begin{displaymath}
\ind_{D\setminus A}
\He_{n}(\gamma V_{A}^{1/2})V_{A}^{n/2} \exp\Big(-\dfrac{\gamma^{2}}{2} V_{A}\Big).
\end{displaymath}
The convergence holds both in
$L^{2}(d\PP,\sigma(\Phi),H^{-\eta}(\C))$ 
and almost surely in $H^{-\eta}(\C)$ (for the Sobolev norm) for every $\eta>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem 5 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $\phi$ and $\Eis(f_s)$ be as above with sufficiently large $\Re(s)$. Then we have
		\begin{equation*}
			\int_{[\bar{G}_n]}\phi\cdot\overline{\Eis(f)}\cdot\Eis(f_s)=\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}\int_{\P_i(F)\bs  G_n(\A)}W^{\Q_i}_{\phi_{\Q_i}}\overline{W^{\Q_i}_{\Eis(f)_{\Q_i}}}\Phi(e_n\cdot)|\det|^{1/2+s},
		\end{equation*}
		where the integrals on both sides converge absolutely.

