[Lemma eq:f_c of arXiv:2605.05193, 'Grokability in five inequalities'] As in Nazarov [Nazarov2003], define
\begin{equation}
f(t):=t^{n-1}e^{-t^2/2},\qquad
c:=\Big(\int_0^\infty f(t)\,dt\Big)^{-1}.
\end{equation}
Then for every $n\geq 1$, every measurable $g:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty]$,
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb R^n}\varphi_n(y)\,g(|y|)\,dy
=
c\int_0^\infty f(r)\,g(r)\,dr.
\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:full-residual of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Assume (equation eq:realization-scale-chain of the paper). With the finite base assembly (equation eq:Ubase-finite-expanded of the paper) and the common coefficients (equation eq:Mless-finite-expanded of the paper), the composite source has the exact finite decomposition (equation eq:source-pieces-expanded of the paper) below and
\begin{align}
 \nm{S_{\rm app}^\varepsilon}_\infty
 &\le C\Lambda_\varepsilon
   \left\{\varepsilon^N\delta^{-N-1}+\varepsilon^{T-1}
   +\delta^{-1}\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{\delta}\right)^\beta\right\},
 \\
 \abs{U_{\mathrm{app}}^{\varepsilon,[N]}(\delta)\big|_{\gamma_-}-g^\varepsilon}_{\infty,-}
 &\le C\left\{\delta^{T}+\varepsilon^3+
 \Lambda_\varepsilon\left[\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{\delta}\right)^\beta+e^{-c\frac{\delta}{\varepsilon}}\right]\right\}.

\end{align}
Thus we have
\begin{align}
 \nm{\mathscr R^\varepsilon(\delta)}_\infty
 \le{}&
 C\delta^{T}
 +
 C\varepsilon^3
 +
 C\Lambda_\varepsilon
 \left[
 \left(\frac{\varepsilon}{\delta}\right)^\beta
 +
 e^{-c\frac{\delta}{\varepsilon}}
 \right]+
 C\Lambda_\varepsilon
 \left\{
 \varepsilon^{N-1}\delta^{-N-1}
 +
 \varepsilon^{T-2}
 +
 \varepsilon^{\beta-1}\delta^{-\beta-1}
 \right\}.

\end{align}
Their constants depend only on the fixed polygon, parameter choices, cutoffs, extension and regularization norms, and the finite data norms in Assumption~(ass:primitive-data-comp of the paper), and are independent of $\varepsilon,\delta$.

