body:
[Lemma lem:plbXj of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Under Assumption (assump:initdiff of the paper), for all $T \in [0,\infty)$ and $\xi \in (0,\infty)$,
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{j \in \mathbb{Z}, u \in \mathbb{R}} e^{u\xi}\mathbb{P}( \inf_{0 \leq s \leq T} X_j(s) - x_j \leq -u ) < \infty,
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{j \in \mathbb{Z}, u \in \mathbb{R}} e^{u\xi + c_0(\xi) j} \mathbb{P}( \inf_{0 \leq s \leq T} X_j(s) \leq -u ) < \infty,
\end{equation}
where $c_0(\xi)$ is the quantity appearing in (equation eq:posbd of the paper).

