[Lem 20 of arXiv:2603.28702, 'Distribution of the magnetization of the critical Ising model on sparse random graphs'] For the class $\mathcal{L}_0$ we have $|\mathcal{L}_0|=(r_1-1)!!$ and for any $L_0\in\mathcal{L}_0$,
\begin{equation}
\SL{\substack{G_1,\dots,G_r\\ L=L_0}}T(G_1,\dots,G_r)=(1+o(1))\cdot\text{Var}(X_{\ell,n})^{r_1/2}\cdot\PL{i=3}^s\tilde{\lambda}_i^{r_i}.
\end{equation}
Under the planted measure, the relation is the same except the $\tilde{\lambda_i}$ become $\tilde{\mu}_i$.

