[Prop CT LB UT of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] For all sufficiently small $t > 0$, the following holds.
  For any $x_0 \in M$ and $\lambda \in (0,\infty)$,
  \begin{equation}
    \inf_{\bm{x}\in \hat{B}_*(x_0,c_2 t^{1/d^{\mathrm{min}}_\mathrm{w}})}
    \hat{P}_{\bm{x}}\bigl(C_t > \lambda t^{d_{\mathrm{ct}}}\bigr)
    \geq
    \tilde{c}_1 \exp\!\left(-\tilde{c}_2\lambda^{2/\hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}}^*}\right).
  \end{equation}

