such that, whenever
$\norm{z-z_*}_{E_b}+\norm y_{\mathsf Y_T}\le R\le R_0$, the endpoint
$F_T(z,y)$ is defined and
\begin{align}
 \norm{D_zF_T(z,y)-S_T}_{\cL(E_b,E_b)}
 +\norm{D_yF_T(z,y)\Gamma_T-A_T}_{\cL(\cH_T,E_b)}
