[Lemma lemma_uniform_bound_infty_Omega of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $\xi \in \{-,+\}$. There almost surely exists $m_0$ such that almost surely, for any $m \geq m_0$ and any $k \geq 1$,
\begin{equation*}
    \sum_{(x_1,\dots,x_k) \in \Omega_{m,j(\xi)}} \delta_m^{\frac{15k}{8}}{\mathbb{E}}_{m,j(\xi)}^{\xi}[\sigma_{x_1} \dots \sigma_{x_k}] \leq C_{k,\infty}^{(\xi)}
\end{equation*}
with $\sum_k\frac{h^k}{k!}C_{k,\infty}^{(\xi)} < \infty$ almost surely.

