[Def signed-realizable of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A stochastic choice rule $G \mapsto c_G(\cdot)$ is \textbf{realizable as a $\Pi$-based signed probability mixture} if there is a finitely additive signed probability measure $Q$ on $(\Pi, {\cal D}_\Pi)$ such that for all $E \in \cal F$ and $G \in \cal G$:
\begin{equation} 
c_G(E) = Q([E, G]_\Pi).
\end{equation}

