[Lemma 10 (Stationarity of the conditional-rate marginal generator) of arXiv:2607.20823, 'Fluctuation impossibility results for stochastic burst networks'] For each $i$, define
\begin{equation}
(\overline L_i\psi)(n)
:=
m_i(n)\sum_{k\ge1}p_{i,k}
\bigl[\psi(n+k)-\psi(n)\bigr]
+
\frac{n}{\tau_i}
\bigl[\psi(n-1)-\psi(n)\bigr],

\end{equation}
with the death term omitted when $n=0$.  Then $\pi_i$ is stationary for
$\overline L_i$.  Moreover,
\begin{equation}
        \E_\pi[(L_i g_i)(X)]=0.

\end{equation}

