[Lemma lem:homogeneous of arXiv:2609.00336, 'Critical points of point charge potentials along lines'] Let $k\geq1$ and $p\geq0$. The space of homogeneous polynomials $P(a,b)$ of degree $k$, even in $b$, and satisfying (equation eq:weighted of the paper), i.e. $P_{aa}+P_{bb}+\frac{p}{b}P_b=0$, is one-dimensional. If $P_{k,p}$ is normalized so that the coefficient of $a^k$ is $1$, then $\nabla P_{k,p}$ does not vanish on $\mathbb{R}^2\backslash\{0\}$ and, on the positively oriented unit circle,
		\begin{equation}
			\degmap\left(\frac{\nabla P_{k,p}}{|\nabla P_{k,p}|}\right)=1-k.
		\end{equation}

