body:
[Lemma 10 (Weighted stable array) of arXiv:2608.01674, '\textbf{Limit Theorems for Tempered Linear Processes with Innovations in the Domain of Att'] Let $w_{N,j}\in\mathbb R$, $j\in\mathbb Z$, and define
$
 w_N(y):=w_{N,\floor{Ny}},  y\in\mathbb R.
$
Suppose that, for some $w\in L^\alpha(\mathbb R)$,
\begin{equation}
 \int_{\mathbb R}|w_N(y)-w(y)|^\alpha\,dy\longrightarrow0,

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\max_{j\in\mathbb Z}|w_{N,j}|}{B_N}\longrightarrow0.

\end{equation}
Assume in addition that, for some
$0<\eta<\alpha-1$,
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{N\ge1}\int_{\mathbb R}
 \left\{|w_N(y)|^{\alpha-\eta}
       +|w_N(y)|^{\alpha+\eta}\right\}\,dy<\infty.

\end{equation}
Then, under Assumption~\ref{ass:innovations},
\[
 \frac1{B_N}\sum_{j\in\mathbb Z}w_{N,j}\varepsilon_j
 \xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{d}
 \int_{\mathbb R}w(y)M_\alpha(dy).
\]
For $\alpha=2$, the same result holds with $L^2$ in
\eqref{eq:Lalphaconv}, with $0<\eta<1$ in
\eqref{eq:neighborLp}, and with $M_2$ denoting the Gaussian random
measure.

[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2605.05864, 'Classification and Metrization of Classes of Smooth measures'] For any compact set $K\subset E$ and \(\alpha >0\), there exists \(C_\alpha >0\) such that, for any \(\mu \in \mathcal{S}_0\), 
\begin{eqnarray*}
\mu (K) \le C_\alpha \sqrt{\mathcal{E}_\alpha(U_\alpha(1_K\mu), U_\alpha(1_K\mu))} \le 
C^2_\alpha \left\| U_\alpha (1_K \mu) \right\|_{\infty}
\end{eqnarray*}
In particular \(C_1=\sqrt{\Capa(K)}\) holds.

