[Thm nonle of arXiv:2411.14090, '{\bf Exponential Ergodicity in $\W_1$ for SDEs with Distribution Dependent Noise and Parti'] Assume {\bf(A3)}.
Then there exists a constant $\delta_0>0$ such that when $\kappa<\delta_0$, (equation ddsde levy one of the paper) has a unique invariant probability measure $\mu^\ast\in \mathbb P_1(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and there exists a constant $c,\lambda>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb W_1(P_t^*\eta, \mu^\ast)\leq c\text{\rm{e}}^{-\lambda t}\mathbb W_1(\eta, \mu^\ast),\ \ \eta\in\mathscr P_1(\mathbb R^d),\, t\geq 0.
\end{equation}

