body:
[Defn 8 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] A real valuation $v$ of $K(X)$ is a map $v:K(X)\rightarrow\R\cup\{\infty\}$ such that for every $f,g\in K(X)$, the following hold:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $v(fg)=v(f)+v(g)$.
    \item $v(f+g)\geq \min\{v(f),v(g)\}$.
    \item $v(f)=\infty$ if and only if $f=0$.
\end{enumerate}

