body:
[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] Fix $T,\nu>0$.  Let $K\in\N$, let
$d_1,\dots,d_r$ be distinct integers with
$0\le r\le4$ and $|d_j|\le2\sqrt K$, and suppose
\begin{align*}
 f'(t)=-\nu Kf(t)+\sum_{j=1}^rz_je^{-\nu(K+d_j)t},
\end{align*}
where $z_j$ are constants. Then
\begin{align*}
 \int_0^T|f(t)|^2\dd t
 \ge c_{\nu,T}(1+K)^{-15}
 \left(|f(0)|^2+\sum_{j=1}^r|z_j|^2\right).
\end{align*}
The constant is independent of $K,r,d_j,f(0),z_j$.

