[Theo 4 (Generalized form of the $H^{2|2}$ monotonicity theorem) of arXiv:2603.25536, 'The $H^{2|2}$ monotonicity theorem revisited'] Suppose $F: \mathbb{R}^N \to \mathbb{R}$ is smooth and jointly convex (i.e., it has a positive semi-definite Hessian). Then the integral
\begin{equation*}
    \int F(e^{t_1},\dots,e^{t_N})d\nu_\delta(\bm{t})
\end{equation*}
is non-increasing in each of the edge weights $W_{ij}$ with $i,j\in\{1,\dots,N,\delta\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

