[Lemma L: exponential_K_moment of arXiv:2606.18654, 'Rigidity of infinite exchangeable sequences with Gaussian marginals'] For $n \geq 1$ suppose that $a_1,\ldots, a_n \in \mathbb{R}$ satisfies $M_\eta(a_j) < \infty$ almost surely for all $j=1,\ldots, n$. Then
        \begin{equation*}
            \mathbb{E}\lb{\exp\lp{\sum_{i=1}^n K_\eta(a_i)}} = \mathbb{E}\lb{\exp\lp{\sum_{i=1}^n a_i X_i}}.
        \end{equation*}

