[Lemma 15 (Evaluation of $\eps(\pi\otimes\tilde\chi)$) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] Let $\pi$ be as usual and $\chi\notin E$. Then if $\pi_p=\pi(\tilde\mu_1, \tilde\mu_2)$, we have
		\begin{equation}
			\eps(\pi\otimes\tilde\chi)=\eps(\mu_1\chi)\eps(\mu_2\chi),
		\end{equation}
		And if $\pi_{p}$ is the twist-minimal supercuspidal representation, we have
        \begin{equation}
            \eps(\pi\otimes\tilde\chi)=-\chi(-1)G((\chi\circ N)\bar{\eta}_\pi).
        \end{equation}
        Here $G((\chi\circ N)\bar{\eta}_\pi)$ is a Gau\ss\ sum over $\F_{p^2}$ given by~\eqref{eq: F_p^2 Gauss sum}.

