[Thm main of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Let $\lambda_{i}(N)\ (i=1,2,\ldots,N)$ denote the eigenvalues of our $N\times N$ addition in Eqn.~((eq_betaaddition of the paper)). Assume that ((eq_gamma of the paper)), ((eq_alpha of the paper)) and ((eq_positivekappa of the paper)) hold,  then there exists a positive constant $\tilde{C}$ and a sequence of positive real numbers $\mu_{+}(N)$, such that
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}\left\{\lambda_{i}':=\frac{\lambda_{i}(N)-\mu_{+}(N)N}{N^{\frac{1}{3}}}
    \right\}_{i=1}^{N}\stackrel{d}{=} \tilde{C}\cdot\mathrm{Airy}(\beta),
\end{equation}
the $\mathrm{Airy}(\beta)$ process. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

