   \E\bigl(W_2^{m-a}A(Z_2)(1+Z_2)^m\bigr)\\
 &=m!\sum_{a=0}^m(-1)^a
   [z^{m-a}]A(z)(1+z)^m,
\end{align*}
where \eqref{eq:coefficient-contraction} was used twice.  Therefore
\begin{align*}
\frac1{m!}\E\bigl(A(Z_2)P_4^m\bigr)
 &= [z^m]A(z)(1+z)^m\sum_{a\geq0}(-z)^a\\
 &= [z^m]A(z)(1+z)^{m-1}.
\end{align*}
Terms with $a>m$ cannot affect the coefficient of $z^m$.  Taking $A=1$ and $A=z$ gives the stated","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:3564012f2f15fe687c53bfc2bf1574da7f126084d4ec36a55d9d0bb769d9d656","revision_digest":"sha256:ba8319d7c0a6d24d60ad70040d8eab388d544e7462d6899ad297f5703c564bcb","source_id":"arxiv:2607.18186","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

