[Lemma eq:useful_bound_1 of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:useful_bounds}
    Let $\alpha \in(0,2)$ and $\delta \in (\max(0, 1-\alpha),2-\alpha)$.

    For all $c > 0$ we can choose $r_0$ sufficiently large such that  for all $i \geq 1$

    \begin{align}

        \varepsilon_i 
        \kappa_{i,j} 
        r_{i-1}^{d(2 - \alpha - \delta)} 
        & \geq 
        c 
        r_{i}^{d(2 - \alpha - \delta)},
        \\

        (r_i / r_0)^{d(2 -\alpha - \delta)} 
        & \geq 
        c
        \log(e/\varepsilon_{i+1}),
        \\

        \log
        (
            6 
            (
                e 
                \kappa_{i,j}
            )^2
        )
        -
        \kappa_{i,j}
        r_{i-1}^{2d}/r_i^{d \alpha}
        & \geq 
        c
        (r_i/r_0)^{d(2-\alpha-\delta)}.
    \end{align}

