body:
[Theorem mainthm of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] Fix $n \geq 2$. 
Let $K_{\mathrm{PF}}$ be the transition kernel of the Burnside process on $\mathrm{PF}_n$ and let $\pi_{\mathrm{PF}}$ be its stationary distribution. 
Then $\lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}} = \lambda_2(K_{\mathrm{PF}}) = \frac{n}{2(n+1)}$, and for all $t\ge1$, 
\begin{equation}
 \max\left\{
  \frac{n}{n+2}\lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}}^t,\,
  1-\frac{t+\log 3}{\log n}
 \right\}
 \le d_{K_{\mathrm{PF}}}(t)
 \le n\sqrt{\frac{n+1}{2}} \lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}}^{t/2}.

\end{equation}
Consequently, for every fixed $0<\varepsilon<1$,
\[
 t_{\mathrm{mix},K_{\mathrm{PF}}}(\varepsilon)=\Theta_\varepsilon(\log n).
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] There is a unique linear operator $x \mapsto x^*$ from $L(V \otimes V)$ such that
\begin{align*}
(v \otimes w)^* = w \otimes v \quad \text{for all $v,w \in V$.}
\end{align*}
Furthermore, we have $x^{**} = x$ for all $x \in V \otimes V$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem maintheorem_with_simplices of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $f\colon \mathbb N^s \to \mathbb C$ satisfy (mainassumption of the paper) and be real and non-negative or satisfy (upperboundassp of the paper) as well. Assume that the polytope $\cal P$ is bounded, that $\cal F$ is not contained in any coordinate hyperplane, and that $\vec \ell$ is of convergent type for $\cal F$. 
    Dissect the polytope $\cal P$ into simplices and let $S_1,\ldots, S_h$ be those simplices that have exactly $d+1$ vertices in the maximal face $\cal F$, where $d = \dim \cal F$. Let the constants $C_{S_j}$ be as in (lem:simplex_computation of the paper) and $\cal F_{S_j} = \cal F \cap S_j$ for $1\leq j\leq h$.

	Then there exists $\varepsilon > 0$ such that 
    \begin{align*}
\Upsilon(B; \vec 1)
		= c_{\cal P} c_f \Bigl( \prod_{i=1}^s \alpha_i^{-\ell_i} \Bigr) B^a (\log B)^{d+\ell}  +  O_{\vec \varpi, \vec \alpha, \vec \ell}(C_f B^a (\log B)^{d + \ell - \varepsilon}),
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align}
c_{\cal P} = \sum_{j=1}^h C_{S_j} \int_{\cal F_{S_j}} \prod_{i=1}^s t_i^{\ell_i} \,\mathrm d\mu.
\end{align}

