[Corollary cor:4.6 of arXiv:2608.27474, 'Nonlocality of Cover-Time Changes Under Edge Addition'] For every \(G,uv,s\) under consideration,
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
f_s(\lambda)\not\equiv f_s(0)
\quad\text{as a rational function of }\lambda.
}

\end{equation}
More precisely, either
\begin{equation}
f_s(\lambda)=\ell_s\lambda+O(1),\qquad \ell_s>0,

\end{equation}
or \(G,s,u,v\) is (equation eq:4.15 of the paper) and (equation eq:4.24 of the paper) holds.

[Lem 16 of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For all $p \in (0, 1/2]$,
\begin{align*}
    w(p) \coloneqq (1-p)^{1-2p}\,p^{2p} > \frac{2}{5},
    \qquad\text{while}\qquad
    e^{1/2} - \frac{e}{2} < \frac{2}{5}.
\end{align*}

