body:
[Lemma of arXiv:2606.16609, 'On stability of outliers from the circular law'] Set $Q_N(z):=1+b_N^*\mathbf{R}_{N}(z)\mathbf{R}_{N}(z)^*b_N$ for $z \notin Sp (D_N)$ and denote by $\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{N-1}$ the eigenvalues of $D_N$. Then 
   \begin{equation*}
       Q_N(z) \overset{}{=} \prod_{k=1}^{N-1}\left(1+\frac{\lvert X_k\lvert^2}{N\lvert z- \mu_k \lvert^2}\right)
   \end{equation*}
   where $X_1,\ldots,X_{N-1}$ are i.i.d. standard complex Gaussian random variables, independent of $\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{N-1}.$

