to show that $Z = 0$. Define a signed measure $\nu$ by 
\begin{equation}
 \nu(B) = \bigexpec{Z\indicator{B}(X)}
\end{equation} 
for any Borel set $B$ of $\R$. The fact that $\expec{Z\e^{tX}} = 0$
means that the Laplace transform of $\nu$  
