{"artifact_digest":"sha256:ccde0f64bffab08cca5998b2154e1d0925d85f17c08ecca0b1ccc57116a7134b","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/cc/ccde0f64bffab08cca5998b2154e1d0925d85f17c08ecca0b1ccc57116a7134b.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:13a8d0a1bf2dc1abbcdeaadb9eb7d475a01e770ac971acd62dabd86b6ae3fbe4","bundle_entry_key":"p0050-square-gap-singularity","bundle_id":"population.w335-p0050-20261010","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"w335/bundle_004.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:probability.random-graphs:negative-correlation-divergent-squared-marginal-gap-singularity","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"For S_N=sum_{i<=N} delta_i X_i and D_N=sum_{i<=N} delta_i^2, the difference of expectations is D_N. Nonnegative weights and nonpositive off-diagonal covariances imply

