[Lemma lem.clock-negnorm of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] Let $s\in(0,1/2]\cap(0,d/2)$ and $\varepsilon>0$. There exists $C_\varepsilon=C_\varepsilon(d,\Lambda,s,\varepsilon,r_0)<\infty$ such that, for every integer $N\ge0$,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{Q}\Bigl(\text{there is an integer }M\ge N\text{ with }\|e^{-2V}-\mathbb{E}[e^{-2V(0)}]\|_{\hat{\phantom{H}}\v@true\h@true\negph@nt{H}\underline{H}^{-s}(\square_M)}>3^{\varepsilon M}\Bigr)\le C_\varepsilon 3^{-2\varepsilon N}\, .
		\end{equation}
		Moreover, for $\mathbb{Q}$-a.e.\ $\omega$, the bound $\|e^{-2V}-\mathbb{E}[e^{-2V(0)}]\|_{\hat{\phantom{H}}\v@true\h@true\negph@nt{H}\underline{H}^{-s}(\square_M)}\le 3^{\varepsilon M}$ holds for all sufficiently large integers $M$.

