[Definition of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] We say that a set $U \subset \Lambda_{M_g+jr,\infty}$ is non-bad if all its elements are either good or mediocre. For a good or mediocre block $\varphi \in \Lambda_{M_g+jr,\infty}$, we define
    \begin{equation*}
        S(\varphi) = \begin{cases}
            |K_{\max}(\varphi)| & \text{ if } \varphi \text{ is good}\\
            \sum_{\varphi^\prime \in \chi_r(\varphi)} |K_{\max}(\varphi^\prime)| & \text{ if } \varphi \text{ is mediocre}
        \end{cases}.
    \end{equation*}

