[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $\alpha \in (0,1/2)$ and $x\in (0,1)$, the following holds
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
U^\varepsilon(x) &= -\frac{1}{h(0)} \log \varepsilon +  \frac{1}{h(0)}  \log \Big(\frac{h(0)}{f(0)} \Big) +  \int_{0}^x \left[ \frac{1}{y h(y)} -\frac{1}{h(0)y} \right] \, dy  +  \frac{1}{h(0)} \log x \\
& + R_{U^\varepsilon} (x) 
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\vert R_{U^\varepsilon} (x) \vert \le C \big[ \varepsilon^{1/2 - \alpha}/ {\mathfrak h}(x) + \varepsilon^{2\alpha}   \big] \ .
\end{split}
\end{equation}

