[Lemma lem:C of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] For $d>2$, there are contants $a_0 > 0$ and $a_1 \in (0,1)$ such that for all $\mu \in (0, 1]$,
\begin{align}

C_\mu(x) \le \frac{ a_0 }{ \nnnorm x^{d-2} } e^{-a_1 m_0(\mu) \norm x _ \infty}
	\qquad(x\in \mathbb Z^d).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.26619, 'Ergodicity of stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on unbounded domains driven by space'] Let $u$ be the solution to the following equation driven by space-time white noise $W$:
\begin{align}
\begin{cases}
    d u(t,x) = \frac{1}{2}\partial_{xx} u(t,x) dt  + W(dt,dx), \quad x\in\mathbb{R},\\
    u(0,x) = f(x), \quad x\in\mathbb{R},
\end{cases}
\end{align}
where $f\in L^p_{\lambda}$ for some $p\geq 1$. 
Then the solution $\{u(t): t\geq 0\}$ is not strong Feller on $L^p_{\lambda}$.

