body:
[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] When flipping a biased coin $n$ times in a row:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $E({\rm heads})=np$.

\item $E({\rm tails})=n(1-p)$.

\item $E(a\times{\rm heads}+b\times{\rm tails})=n(ap+b(1-p))$.
\end{enumerate}

[Corollary cor:bernton47mod of arXiv:2506.03999, 'Large deviations for scaled families of Schr\"odinger bridges with reflection'] ``Let Assumption (ass:bernton44mod of the paper) hold.
    For any open set $G \subseteq \calX_0 \times \calY_0$,
    \begin{equation}
        \liminf_{\eta \downarrow 0} \eta \log \pi_\eta(G) \geq -\inf_{(x,y) \in G} I(x,y).\text{''}
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma l:negligible.BCDE of arXiv:2601.12677, 'Stable and Fréchet limit theorem for subgraph functionals in the hyperbolic random geometr'] In the setting of Proposition (p:exp.clique of the paper), there exist $C, c_0 \in (0,\infty)$, both of which are independent of $n$ and $u$, such that 
\begin{equation*}
B_n(u) + \sum_{\ell=2}^{m-2} C_{n,\ell}(u) + D_n(u) + E_n(u) \le  \begin{cases}
C \beta_n e^{\frac{1}{2} (d-1)u}, & \text{for all } n \ge 1 \text{ and } u \in (0,{\gamma R_n}), \\[3pt]
Ce^{c_0\omega_n} \cdot e^{\frac{1}{2} (d-1)u}, & \text{for all } n \ge 1 \text{ and } u \in (0,R_n), 
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}
for some sequence $\beta_n\to0$.

