[Theorem 33 (Scaling law, mixed-damping regime) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:diagonal-covariance} and~\ref{ass:power-law}, assuming the stability condition \(\eta\lesssim\min\{1, B^\beta(1-\rho)\}\), for the mixed-damping regime $\eta\gtrsim(1-\rho)^2$ with $k \gtrsim \max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho}, \frac{1-\rho}{\eta}\right\}$, the expected excess risk satisfies:
\begin{equation}

    \EE[\cE(\btheta_k)] \eqsim \cS_{\mathrm{under}}(k) + \left(\frac{1-\rho}{\eta k}\right)^s + \frac{\sigma^2}{B} \min\left\{ \left(\frac{\eta}{1-\rho}\right)^{\frac1\beta}, \frac{\eta}{1-\rho} \right\},
\end{equation}
where the properties of the underdamped transient $\cS_{\mathrm{under}}(k)$ are established in Lemma~\ref{lem:nes_underdamped_transient_properties}.

