body:
[Lemma 54 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the notation in Lemma \ref{Lem.PowerSeriesSG}. There exist constants $\delta_2 \in (0,\delta_0]$ and $\epsilon_2 > 0$, depending on $q, \kappa, c$, such that for $r \in [0, \delta_2]$
\begin{equation}
\Real \left [\GFt(z) - \GFt(c) \right] \geq \epsilon_2 \cdot r^2, \mbox{ if } z = c + r e^{\pm \im \pi/2}.
\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:delta of arXiv:2608.30888, 'Three-term asymptotics for discrete\\ Hardy--Rellich constants in high dimension'] For every fixed $\ell\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
 \mu_{\ell,N}
 =2^\ell N^\ell+\gamma_\ell N^{\ell-1}
  +\delta_\ell N^{\ell-2}+O_\ell(N^{\ell-3}),
\end{equation}
where $\delta_\ell$ is given by (equation eq:delta of the paper).  Its first values are
\[
 \delta_1=-\frac{20}{3},\qquad
 \delta_2=-\frac{7729}{540},\qquad
 \delta_3=-\frac{30020}{4459},\qquad
 \delta_4=\frac{5639018}{57375}.
\]

