[Prop q3_min_lemma of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] Let $Y$ be an integer homology sphere and $L\subseteq Y$ be an integrally-framed link whose linking matrix has determinant $\pm 1$. 
	Let $W\colon Y \to Y'$ denote the trace of $L$.
	Then if $Y$ is $q_3$-minimal, we have
    \begin{equation}
        q_3(Y') - q_3(Y) \ge -b^+(W),
    \end{equation}
    and if $Y$ is $q_3$-maximal, we have
      \begin{equation}
        q_3(Y') - q_3(Y) \le b^-(W).
    \end{equation}
    In particular, both inequalities hold if $Y=S^3$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

