body:
[Theorem 58 (Kolmogorov continuity criterion) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] Let $(\phi(x))_{x\in[0,L]}$ be a stochastic process such that 
\begin{equation}
 \bigexpec{\norm{\phi(y) - \phi(x)}^\mu} 
 \leqs C \abs{y-x}^{1+\nu}
\end{equation} 
for all $x,y\in[0,L]$, for some constants $\mu, \nu>0$. Then 
there exists a modification of the process $(\phi(x))_{x\in[0,L]}$ whose 
paths belong to $\cC^\alpha$ for all $\alpha < \frac{\nu}{\mu}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 17 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $\phi^{(y)}_n$ be as in (\ref{producsequencegeneral}) for every $n\geq 1$. Then, for any finite $y\in\R_+\setminus\{0\}$,
\begin{align}
\phi^{(y)}_n \rightarrow \frac{y^2}{2} \,\,\, \text{as} \,\,\, n \rightarrow \infty. \notag
\end{align}

