body:
[Corollary 37 of arXiv:2604.26549, 'Existence and uniqueness results of a stochastic nonlinear heat equation with a constraint'] Let $\wtilde{M}$ be the process defined in \eqref{eqn-martingale-1}. Then, for $t\in[0, T]$, the quadratic variation of $\wtilde{M}$ is given by
				\begin{align}
					\llbracket \wtilde{M}\rrbracket_t=\int_0^t\sum_{i=1}^M\|\Nn_i(u(s))\|_{L^2(\bO)}^2ds.
				\end{align}
